/-!
# Finite presentation near a contracted prime after field extension

Source: Stacks Project, Varieties, Tag 0C4Y (lemma-change-fields-flat), assertion (1),
and Algebra, Tag 00R2 (lemma-finite-presentation-independent); the agent-written
finite-relation consequence conditional on module-neighbourhood surjectivity
(blueprint: lem-sc-finite-presentation-field-extension-neighbourhood).

The scalar-extension map is the tensor product of the specified `k`-algebra map
with the identity of `K`. Finite type and finite presentation are predicates on
these specified ring maps, without choosing additional algebra structures.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w z

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace AlgHom

/-- Finite presentation on a principal open after field extension descends near
its contracted prime, assuming the module-neighbourhood surjectivity principle.
Source: Stacks Project, Varieties, Tag 0C4Y (1), and Algebra, Tag 00R2;
agent-written conditional finite-relation consequence
(blueprint: lem-sc-finite-presentation-field-extension-neighbourhood).

In `hdescent`, `(C tensor_k K) tensor_C M` is the canonical model of `M tensor_k K`
used by `LinearMap.exists_localizedMap_away_surjective_of_fieldExtension`:
`(c tensor lambda) tensor m` corresponds to `(c • m) tensor lambda`.
The test rings and modules live in a common universe containing all input rings;
this admits arbitrary test objects at the size needed for the polynomial
presentation, its ideal of relations and the finite free module mapping onto it.
The condition on `s` is exactly exclusion from the contracted prime.

Proof, following the node's six steps:
1. Finite type gives a surjection `T = A[x_1,...,x_n] → B` with kernel `I`.
   Identify `T tensor_k K` with `(A tensor_k K)[x_1,...,x_n]` by the monomial
   formula `(a x^nu) tensor lambda ↦ (a tensor lambda) x^nu`, with its inverse
   given by the reverse formula; this uses the finite-type and polynomial
   definitions and the tensor-product construction.
2. `lem-weil-pbc-module-over-field-flat` and `lem-weil-pbc-flat-tensor-exact`
   identify `I tensor_k K` with the kernel `I_K` of `T_K → B_K`. Its image is
   generated by `f tensor 1` for `f` in `I`. Lift `u` to `v` in `T_K`; the inverse
   image `P` of `qK` is prime and does not contain `v`.
3. By `lem-weil-pbc-localization-away-polynomial-quotient`, adjoining `y = 1/u`
   presents `(B_K)_u` as the quotient of `T_K[y]` by `H = I_K[y] + (vy - 1)`.
   Its finite presentation and
   `lem-weil-pbc-finite-presentation-surjection-kernel-fg` give finitely many
   generators of `H`.
4. Expand these generators in `I_K[y] + (vy - 1)` and expand their finitely many
   coefficients from `I_K` as sums of tensors from `I`. Collect finitely many
   `f_i` in `I`. Evaluation at `y = 1/v` proves that the `f_i tensor 1` generate
   `(I_K)_v`. The localization fraction criterion proves that this localized
   ideal embeds in `(T_K)_v`, identifying its image with the extended ideal.
5. Apply `hdescent`, the principle of
   `lem-sc-module-surjectivity-field-extension-neighbourhood`, to the map
   `T^r → I` given by the `f_i`, localized upstairs at `v`. Obtain `d` in `T`
   outside the contraction of `P` such that `I_d` is generated by the `f_i`.
   Its image `s` in `B` is outside the contraction of `qK`.
6. `lem-weil-pbc-localization-quotient-commute` identifies `B_s` with `T_d/I_d`.
   The localization-away polynomial presentation then gives the finite
   presentation `A[x_1,...,x_n,y]/(f_1,...,f_r,dy - 1)` of `B_s`. -/
theorem exists_finitePresentation_away_of_fieldExtension
    {k : Type u} {K : Type v} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    {A : Type w} {B : Type z} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra k A] [Algebra k B]
    (hdescent : ∀ (C : Type (max u v w z)) [CommRing C] [Algebra k C]
      (M N : Type (max u v w z)) [AddCommGroup M] [AddCommGroup N]
      [Module C M] [Module C N] (φ : M →ₗ[C] N)
      (v : C ⊗[k] K) (P : Ideal (C ⊗[k] K)) [P.IsPrime],
      v ∉ P →
      Function.Surjective
        (LocalizedModule.map (Submonoid.powers v) (φ.baseChange (C ⊗[k] K))) →
      ∃ d : C, algebraMap C (C ⊗[k] K) d ∉ P ∧
        Function.Surjective (LocalizedModule.map (Submonoid.powers d) φ))
    (α : A →ₐ[k] B) (qK : Ideal (B ⊗[k] K)) [qK.IsPrime]
    (u : B ⊗[k] K) (hu : u ∉ qK) (hfinite : α.toRingHom.FiniteType)
    (hfp : ((algebraMap (B ⊗[k] K) (Localization.Away u)).comp
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.map α (AlgHom.id k K)).toRingHom).FinitePresentation) :
    ∃ s : B, algebraMap B (B ⊗[k] K) s ∉ qK ∧
      ((algebraMap B (Localization.Away s)).comp α.toRingHom).FinitePresentation := by
  sorry

end AlgHom
